{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-73589e9e-64df-4663-bb82-e89f8055c5fc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a477a9def0c43110","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-2wenprbp/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Manager binary reconciliation error log conversion to structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nConverts reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator **manager binary** from\nmessage-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs, and adds the `resourceKind`\nstructured field across every controller tier. Today most reconciliation error logs embed the\nresource name and namespace in the message string (for example\n`log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile Dashboard 'example' in namespace 'redhat-ods-applications'\")`),\nwhich prevents operators from querying logs by resource name or namespace. After this epic, every\nreconciliation error log in the manager binary emits `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as\nstructured logr key-value pairs using camelCase keys, and the DSCInitialization controller's\nnon-standard key names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) are migrated to the same convention.\n\n## Scope\n\n- **Audit**: identify every `log.Error()` call site in the manager binary's reconciliation error\n  paths via grep/static analysis, tracked in a checklist with a per-site disposition (converted\n  or explicitly exempted with reason). This also validates the strategy's 75%\n  embedded-identity estimate.\n- **Identity conversion**: for each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the\n  message string, extract the identity into structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`)\n  and remove the redundant identity from the message text.\n- **`resourceKind` addition** across all manager controller tiers:\n  - DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller and the 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines,\n    Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI)\n  - Module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX,\n    Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator)\n  - DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller\n  - 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup)\n- **Action files**: convert and add `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` in all 15 action files\n  across the four tiers — 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`),\n  3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`),\n  1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), and\n  3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n- **DSCI key migration**: replace the non-standard `Request.Name` / `DSCInitialization`\n  structured field names with `name` / `namespace` / `resourceKind`.\n- **Cluster-scoped resources** (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit `name` and\n  `resourceKind`; `namespace` is omitted or set to empty string, never a spurious value.\n- **CI lint rule (manager-binary portion)**: author and verify the part of the CI lint rule /\n  static-analysis check covering the manager binary's converted call sites — it flags any\n  `log.Error` call in the manager binary that embeds name/namespace in message text or is\n  missing the required structured fields.\n- **Unit tests**: assert field presence and correctness by parsing test logger output for each\n  controller tier and action file tier.\n- **Backwards-compatibility verification**: before/after log output comparison for a sample\n  reconciliation error from a dev-cluster test build with the production log consumer stack\n  configured; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify and update text-based alert rules that\n  rely on message-string patterns.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. A tracked audit checklist covering 100% of grep/static-analysis-identified `log.Error` call\n   sites in the manager binary's reconciliation error paths exists, with every site dispositioned\n   (converted, or exempted with a stated reason).\n2. Static analysis over the manager binary reports zero `log.Error` calls in reconciliation\n   error paths that embed resource name or namespace in the message string — all such call sites\n   emit `name` and `namespace` as structured key-value pairs.\n3. A codebase grep confirms no remaining references to the non-standard DSCI field names\n   (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) in DSCI error-log paths, and a unit test asserts DSCI\n   error logs contain `name` and `namespace` with correct values.\n4. Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with the correct value\n   for all 5 service controllers, the module controller and its 8 module handlers, the DSC\n   controller, and the 8 component controllers.\n5. Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with correct values\n   across all 15 action files (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module).\n6. Unit tests confirm cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) emit\n   `name` and `resourceKind` and do not emit a spurious namespace value (omitted or empty).\n7. The CI lint rule portion covering the manager binary's converted call sites is authored and\n   verified: it passes on the converted codebase and flags an injected violation (a `log.Error`\n   call embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields).\n8. A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms the\n   structured fields appear and the production-configured log consumer ingests both formats\n   without configuration changes, and message-pattern-dependent alert rules identified in\n   coordination with SRE/Support are updated.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — name/namespace structured KV conversion of message-embedded identity\n  (manager binary share).\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — DSCI controller migrated from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to the\n  camelCase convention.\n- **HLR-3 (P0)** — all service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator,\n  Setup) reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`.\n- **HLR-4 (P0)** — all 15 action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`\n  across all 4 tiers.\n- **HLR-6 (P0)** — module controller error logs (8 module handlers) include `name`,\n  `namespace`, `resourceKind`.\n- **HLR-7 (P1, bundled)** — DSC and component controller `resourceKind` is added to the same\n  `log.Error` call sites in the same files converted for the P0 HLRs; a separate epic would\n  re-edit and re-audit the same files twice, so the work is not separately schedulable and is\n  kept bundled here.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The audit may reveal more embedded-identity call sites than the strategy's 75% estimate;\n  the checklist makes the actual count visible (see the decomposition summary's re-split\n  trigger if the volume pushes this epic past its estimate).\n- SRE/Support turnaround for identifying and updating text-based alert rules is externally\n  controlled and may extend calendar time without indicating incomplete engineering work.\n- Log message strings change (identity removed after moving to structured fields); ingestion\n  compatibility is verified before merge per the backwards-compatibility NFR.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":67327,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b612d40fa2f9fe03","agent_id":"a7bb47802f7b4a7f4","session_id":"d69bb09f-72b1-4df0-bf0b-d16ae9dbfdec","uuid":"efd1feef-deac-4c97-ae1a-e677f64fbdc4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:34:36.362Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
