{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e2b61520-4948-4190-8f8d-01cea2f9eec5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1ae4da957f2b2a6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-2wenprbp/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E002.md","content":"# Cloudmanager binary reconciliation error log conversion to structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nConverts reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator **cloudmanager binary** — the\ncompanion binary that handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies on AWS EKS, Azure AKS, and\nCoreWeave — from message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs, and adds the\n`resourceKind` structured field. The cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine,\nAzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the same controller-runtime/logr\nfoundation using the shared reconciler pattern, so they already receive `name` and `namespace`\nfrom the request logger; the remaining work is converting any error paths that still embed\nresource identity in message strings and adding `resourceKind` (the kind is not implied by the\ncontroller name for queryability across the three engine kinds).\n\n## Scope\n\n- **Audit**: identify every `log.Error()` call site in the cloudmanager binary's reconciliation\n  error paths via grep/static analysis, tracked in a checklist with a per-site disposition\n  (converted or explicitly exempted with reason).\n- **Identity conversion**: for each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the\n  message string, extract the identity into structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n- **`resourceKind` addition**: all three cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine,\n  AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) emit `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`\n  as structured fields in reconciliation error logs.\n- **CI lint rule (cloudmanager-binary portion)**: author and verify the part of the CI lint\n  rule / static-analysis check covering the cloudmanager binary's converted call sites — it\n  flags any `log.Error` call in the cloudmanager binary that embeds name/namespace in message\n  text or is missing the required structured fields.\n- **Unit tests**: assert field presence and correctness by parsing test logger output for each\n  cloudmanager controller.\n- **Backwards-compatibility verification**: before/after log output comparison for a sample\n  reconciliation error, confirming the production log consumer (e.g. CloudWatch on the\n  non-OpenShift Kubernetes deployments) ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. A tracked audit checklist covering 100% of grep/static-analysis-identified `log.Error` call\n   sites in the cloudmanager binary's reconciliation error paths exists, with every site\n   dispositioned (converted, or exempted with a stated reason).\n2. Unit tests parsing test logger output assert that all three cloudmanager controllers\n   (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) emit `name`,\n   `namespace`, and `resourceKind` with correct values on reconciliation errors, and static\n   analysis reports zero remaining `log.Error` calls embedding resource identity in message\n   text.\n3. The CI lint rule portion covering the cloudmanager binary's converted call sites is authored\n   and verified: it passes on the converted codebase and flags an injected violation (a\n   `log.Error` call embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields).\n4. A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms the\n   structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration\n   changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-5 (P0)** — all cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine,\n  CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and\n  `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — name/namespace structured KV conversion of message-embedded identity\n  (cloudmanager binary share; the strategy's component rhods-operator spans both binaries).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Release timing for the cloudmanager binary (same release as the manager work or a subsequent\n  release) is a PM decision; the strategy notes cloudmanager is only deployed on non-OpenShift\n  Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave), so its impact scope is narrower. The work itself is\n  unchanged either way; this epic's boundary allows it to follow a later release train without\n  restructuring.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":69082,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b612d40fa2f9fe03","agent_id":"a7bb47802f7b4a7f4","session_id":"d69bb09f-72b1-4df0-bf0b-d16ae9dbfdec","uuid":"cde08705-9ec9-4176-bcd6-6c10b3623127","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:34:48.997Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
