{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf0f31e502398402","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Cloudmanager binary reconciliation error log conversion to structured resource\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Cloudmanager binary reconciliation error log conversion to structured resource context\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tConverts reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator **cloudmanager binary** — the\n35\tcompanion binary that handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies on AWS EKS, Azure AKS, and\n36\tCoreWeave — from message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs, and adds the\n37\t`resourceKind` structured field. The cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine,\n38\tAzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the same controller-runtime/logr\n39\tfoundation using the shared reconciler pattern, so they already receive `name` and `namespace`\n40\tfrom the request logger; the remaining work is converting any error paths that still embed\n41\tresource identity in message strings and adding `resourceKind` (the kind is not implied by the\n42\tcontroller name for queryability across the three engine kinds).\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- **Audit**: identify every `log.Error()` call site in the cloudmanager binary's reconciliation\n47\t  error paths via grep/static analysis, tracked in a checklist with a per-site disposition\n48\t  (converted or explicitly exempted with reason).\n49\t- **Identity conversion**: for each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the\n50\t  message string, extract the identity into structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n51\t- **`resourceKind` addition**: all three cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine,\n52\t  AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) emit `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`\n53\t  as structured fields in reconciliation error logs.\n54\t- **CI lint rule (cloudmanager-binary portion)**: author and verify the part of the CI lint\n55\t  rule / static-analysis check covering the cloudmanager binary's converted call sites — it\n56\t  flags any `log.Error` call in the cloudmanager binary that embeds name/namespace in message\n57\t  text or is missing the required structured fields.\n58\t- **Unit tests**: assert field presence and correctness by parsing test logger output for each\n59\t  cloudmanager controller.\n60\t- **Backwards-compatibility verification**: before/after log output comparison for a sample\n61\t  reconciliation error, confirming the production log consumer (e.g. CloudWatch on the\n62\t  non-OpenShift Kubernetes deployments) ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t1. A tracked audit checklist covering 100% of grep/static-analysis-identified `log.Error` call\n67\t   sites in the cloudmanager binary's reconciliation error paths exists, with every site\n68\t   dispositioned (converted, or exempted with a stated reason).\n69\t2. Unit tests parsing test logger output assert that all three cloudmanager controllers\n70\t   (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) emit `name`,\n71\t   `namespace`, and `resourceKind` with correct values on reconciliation errors, and static\n72\t   analysis reports zero remaining `log.Error` calls embedding resource identity in message\n73\t   text.\n74\t3. The CI lint rule portion covering the cloudmanager binary's converted call sites is authored\n75\t   and verified: it passes on the converted codebase and flags an injected violation (a\n76\t   `log.Error` call embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields).\n77\t4. A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms the\n78\t   structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration\n79\t   changes.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- **HLR-5 (P0)** — all cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine,\n84\t  CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and\n85\t  `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n86\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — name/namespace structured KV conversion of message-embedded identity\n87\t  (cloudmanager binary share; the strategy's component rhods-operator spans both binaries).\n88\t\n89\t## Risks / Notes\n90\t\n91\t- Release timing for the cloudmanager binary (same release as the manager work or a subsequent\n92\t  release) is a PM decision; the strategy notes cloudmanager is only deployed on non-OpenShift\n93\t  Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave), so its impact scope is narrower. The work itself is\n94\t  unchanged either way; this epic's boundary allows it to follow a later release train without\n95\t  restructuring.\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acd72c9b7361e749","agent_id":"ac4cb35322e159ee0","session_id":"d69bb09f-72b1-4df0-bf0b-d16ae9dbfdec","uuid":"b30d2bc2-11ee-421a-a3e5-35da2e648448","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:36:38.971Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf0f31e502398402","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
