ort exceeds ~1.5 sprints → split\n61\tby controller tier) — the defensible shape (b); not docked, no split demanded. No scope\n62\tduplication: the CI lint rule is correctly divided per surface into E001's and E002's Scope/ACs\n63\trather than extracted as a standalone enforcement epic — the compliant shape. No epic mixes code\n64\timplementation with content authoring.\n65\t\n66\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n67\tAll three epics are Implementation producing concrete artifacts (converted code + tests +\n68\tlint-rule coverage; guideline + publication + tracking issues). The Investigation Assessment\n69\tdischarges each strategy unknown with a reasoned \"does not change epic structure\" disposition\n70\t(extended fields → E003 disposition AC; alert inventory → embedded in E001's verification AC;\n71\tcloudmanager release timing → scheduling only; audit percentage → each epic's own checklist\n72\twork) — none warrants an Investigation, so no `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` fields are needed\n73\tand none are set. E003's classification as a general Implementation rather than `docs-authoring`\n74\tis justified: it is a repo-level contribution guideline plus an external publication spec, not a\n75\tRed Hat docs content-process deliverable, and the strategy's Documentation Support gate reads\n76\t\"Pending human review\" (template placeholder), not \"Yes\" — so Rule 11 docs-last routing does not\n77\tapply (validator confirms).\n78\t\n79\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n80\tAll three Implementation epics carry `ai_signals` (type-appropriate field; `investigation_signals`\n81\tcorrectly null) and each has an ai-signals file whose rationales match the frontmatter values.\n82\tSpot-checks hold up: E001 `human_process_gates: -1` is justified by the SRE/Support alert-rule\n83\tcoordination embedded in its verification AC; E003 `external_dependency: -1` matches the COO\n84\ttracking-issue filing in its scope; E003 `existing_foundation: 0` is right for a greenfield\n