{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca286359862f014","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Manager binary reconciliation error log conversion to structured resource context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Manager binary reconciliation error log conversion to structured resource context\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tConverts reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator **manager binary** from\n34\tmessage-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs, and adds the `resourceKind`\n35\tstructured field across every controller tier. Today most reconciliation error logs embed the\n36\tresource name and namespace in the message string (for example\n37\t`log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile Dashboard 'example' in namespace 'redhat-ods-applications'\")`),\n38\twhich prevents operators from querying logs by resource name or namespace. After this epic, every\n39\treconciliation error log in the manager binary emits `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as\n40\tstructured logr key-value pairs using camelCase keys, and the DSCInitialization controller's\n41\tnon-standard key names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) are migrated to the same convention.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- **Audit**: identify every `log.Error()` call site in the manager binary's reconciliation error\n46\t  paths via grep/static analysis, tracked in a checklist with a per-site disposition (converted\n47\t  or explicitly exempted with reason). This also validates the strategy's 75%\n48\t  embedded-identity estimate.\n49\t- **Identity conversion**: for each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the\n50\t  message string, extract the identity into structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`)\n51\t  and remove the redundant identity from the message text.\n52\t- **`resourceKind` addition** across all manager controller tiers:\n53\t  - DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller and the 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines,\n54\t    Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI)\n55\t  - Module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX,\n56\t    Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator)\n57\t  - DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller\n58\t  - 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup)\n59\t- **Action files**: convert and add `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` in all 15 action files\n60\t  across the four tiers — 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`),\n61\t  3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`),\n62\t  1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), and\n63\t  3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n64\t- **DSCI key migration**: replace the non-standard `Request.Name` / `DSCInitialization`\n65\t  structured field names with `name` / `namespace` / `resourceKind`.\n66\t- **Cluster-scoped resources** (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit `name` and\n67\t  `resourceKind`; `namespace` is omitted or set to empty string, never a spurious value.\n68\t- **CI lint rule (manager-binary portion)**: author and verify the part of the CI lint rule /\n69\t  static-analysis check covering the manager binary's converted call sites — it flags any\n70\t  `log.Error` call in the manager binary that embeds name/namespace in message text or is\n71\t  missing the required structured fields.\n72\t- **Unit tests**: assert field presence and correctness by parsing test logger output for each\n73\t  controller tier and action file tier.\n74\t- **Backwards-compatibility verification**: before/after log output comparison for a sample\n75\t  reconciliation error from a dev-cluster test build with the production log consumer stack\n76\t  configured; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify and update text-based alert rules that\n77\t  rely on message-string patterns.\n78\t\n79\t## Acceptance Criteria\n80\t\n81\t1. A tracked audit checklist covering 100% of grep/static-analysis-identified `log.Error` call\n82\t   sites in the manager binary's reconciliation error paths exists, with every site dispositioned\n83\t   (converted, or exempted with a stated reason).\n84\t2. Static analysis over the manager binary reports zero `log.Error` calls in reconciliation\n85\t   error paths that embed resource name or namespace in the message string — all such call sites\n86\t   emit `name` and `namespace` as structured key-value pairs.\n87\t3. A codebase grep confirms no remaining references to the non-standard DSCI field names\n88\t   (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) in DSCI error-log paths, and a unit test asserts DSCI\n89\t   error logs contain `name` and `namespace` with correct values.\n90\t4. Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with the correct value\n91\t   for all 5 service controllers, the module controller and its 8 module handlers, the DSC\n92\t   controller, and the 8 component controllers.\n93\t5. Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with correct values\n94\t   across all 15 action files (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module).\n95\t6. Unit tests confirm cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) emit\n96\t   `name` and `resourceKind` and do not emit a spurious namespace value (omitted or empty).\n97\t7. The CI lint rule portion covering the manager binary's converted call sites is authored and\n98\t   verified: it passes on the converted codebase and flags an injected violation (a `log.Error`\n99\t   call embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields).\n100\t8. A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms the\n101\t   structured fields appear and the production-configured log consumer ingests both formats\n102\t   without configuration changes, and message-pattern-dependent alert rules identified in\n103\t   coordination with SRE/Support are updated.\n104\t\n105\t## HLR Traceability\n106\t\n107\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — name/namespace structured KV conversion of message-embedded identity\n108\t  (manager binary share).\n109\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — DSCI controller migrated from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to the\n110\t  camelCase convention.\n111\t- **HLR-3 (P0)** — all service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator,\n112\t  Setup) reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`.\n113\t- **HLR-4 (P0)** — all 15 action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`\n114\t  across all 4 tiers.\n115\t- **HLR-6 (P0)** — module controller error logs (8 module handlers) include `name`,\n116\t  `namespace`, `resourceKind`.\n117\t- **HLR-7 (P1, bundled)** — DSC and component controller `resourceKind` is added to the same\n118\t  `log.Error` call sites in the same files converted for the P0 HLRs; a separate epic would\n119\t  re-edit and re-audit the same files twice, so the work is not separately schedulable and is\n120\t  kept bundled here.\n121\t\n122\t## Risks / Notes\n123\t\n124\t- The audit may reveal more embedded-identity call sites than the strategy's 75% estimate;\n125\t  the checklist makes the actual count visible (see the decomposition summary's re-split\n126\t  trigger if the volume pushes this epic past its estimate).\n127\t- SRE/Support turnaround for identifying and updating text-based alert rules is externally\n128\t  controlled and may extend calendar time without indicating incomplete engineering work.\n129\t- Log message strings change (identity removed after moving to structured fields); ingestion\n130\t  compatibility is verified before merge per the backwards-compatibility NFR.\n131\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-857ead3cbe10d32a","agent_id":"a60ddb101ee3fd566","session_id":"d69bb09f-72b1-4df0-bf0b-d16ae9dbfdec","uuid":"8ac5dcf1-7805-42cd-b288-60904512136f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:40:54.557Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca286359862f014","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010"}
