{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88c811e259cd7ffd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: Structured log field convention guideline and external operator publication\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 0\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: -1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Structured log field convention guideline and external operator publication\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tAuthors and publishes the structured log field convention as a contribution guideline for new\n34\tcontroller development in the rhods-operator, and publishes it externally so that operators\n35\toutside RHOAI's control (the Cluster Observability Operator team's Loki Operator and Tempo\n36\tOperator) can adopt it voluntarily. The guideline documents the required structured fields\n37\t(`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem\n38\tdiagnosis behind the strategy (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys, missing\n39\t`resourceKind`), with before/after code examples and a DSCI key-name migration guide. This is\n40\tsubstantive content authoring — a distinct work stream from the code conversion — and it is\n41\tintentionally publishable early: the convention is fully specified by the strategy's Staff\n42\tEngineer input, so it does not wait for the code conversion to complete.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- **Contribution guideline** (the design doc the strategy lists as \"to be created\"),\n47\t  covering:\n48\t  - Required structured fields for reconciliation error logs: `name`, `namespace`,\n49\t    `resourceKind`, with cluster-scoped-resource guidance (namespace omitted or empty).\n50\t  - camelCase naming rationale, aligned with controller-runtime's structured log key\n51\t    conventions.\n52\t  - The three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys\n53\t    (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and missing `resourceKind`.\n54\t  - Before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured\n55\t    key-value pairs.\n56\t  - DSCI key-name migration guide with before/after query examples for operators who have\n57\t    existing Loki/CloudWatch queries filtering on the old field names, noting that the\n58\t    transition lands in a single release.\n59\t  - The disposition of extended fields beyond name/namespace/kind (e.g. reconciliation\n60\t    attempt count, error category): included, or explicitly deferred with the PM /\n61\t    Observability decision point recorded.\n62\t- **External publication**: publish the convention as a specification for voluntary adoption by\n63\t  external operator teams, and file tracking issues in the Cluster Observability Operator team's\n64\t  Loki Operator and Tempo Operator projects. Per platform policy overlay 0008, RHOAI does not\n65\t  install, manage, or control external operator dependencies — adoption is at the COO team's\n66\t  discretion and is not gated by this work.\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t1. A contribution guideline is published in the rhods-operator repository specifying the\n71\t   required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming\n72\t   rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI\n73\t   keys, missing `resourceKind`).\n74\t2. The guideline includes before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity\n75\t   to structured key-value pairs, and a DSCI key-name migration guide with before/after query\n76\t   examples.\n77\t3. The guideline explicitly states the disposition of extended fields beyond\n78\t   name/namespace/resourceKind (included in the convention, or deferred with the decision point\n79\t   recorded).\n80\t4. The convention is published for external operator adoption, and tracking issues are filed\n81\t   in the Cluster Observability Operator team's Loki Operator and Tempo Operator projects.\n82\t5. The guideline is technically reviewed for accuracy against the rhods-operator codebase\n83\t   (field names, controller structure, controller-runtime/logr key conventions).\n84\t\n85\t## HLR Traceability\n86\t\n87\t- **HLR-8 (P1)** — document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller\n88\t  development and publish for external operator adoption.\n89\t\n90\t## Risks / Notes\n91\t\n92\t- External adoption timing is outside RHOAI's control (platform policy overlay 0008); filing\n93\t  tracking issues and publishing early is the mitigation, and best-effort adoption is the\n94\t  accepted outcome — no RHOAI-side deliverable is gated on the COO team.\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-857ead3cbe10d32a","agent_id":"a60ddb101ee3fd566","session_id":"d69bb09f-72b1-4df0-bf0b-d16ae9dbfdec","uuid":"d13e6157-8815-46cd-895b-63438e4cbfe9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:40:55.720Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88c811e259cd7ffd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010"}
